---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PromptBlock from '../../components/PromptBlock.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Finance cookbook · Pace"
  description="Finance recipes for the Pace marketplace. Month-end as a workflow. Variance you have to explain, surfaced before the CFO asks. Vendor contract triage that respects the playbook."
  activeNav="cookbook"
  canonicalPath="/cookbook/finance"
>
  <article class="usecases-page">
    <header class="usecases-team-page-head">
      <a class="usecases-back-link" href="/cookbook">&larr; All cookbooks</a>
      <span class="usecases-eyebrow">Finance cookbook</span>
      <h1>Finance</h1>
      <p class="usecases-team-page-tagline">Month-end as a workflow. Variance you have to explain, surfaced before the CFO asks. Vendor contract triage that respects the playbook.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="usecases-team-page-body">
<article class="usecase-card usecase-card-marquee">
        <span class="usecase-card-badge">Marquee recipe</span>
        <h3>Month-end runbook, automated</h3>
        <p class="usecase-outcome">Half a day saved every close, every month.</p>
        <dl class="usecase-meta">
          <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Routine, schedule, monthly on the last business day at 08:00</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>close-management</code>, <code>reconciliation</code>, <code>variance-analysis</code>, <code>journal-entry-prep</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Routines (cloud schedule), warehouse + Microsoft 365 connectors, plan mode for the journal entries</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p>The month-end runbook fires automatically on the last business day. By the time the controller sits down, the reconciliation has run, variance vs plan is drafted, and the journal entries are queued for approval in plan mode. Half a day saved every close.</p>

        <div class="usecase-setup">
          <h4 class="usecase-setup-title">How to set it up</h4>
          <ol class="usecase-steps">
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">1</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Install the finance plugin</h5>
                <div class="usecase-step-actions">
                  <a class="usecase-step-btn" href="https://claude.ai/desktop/customize/plugins/new?marketplace=GoldenBerry-SO/Pace&plugin=finance" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Install in Cowork &nearr;</a>
                  <code class="usecase-step-cmd">claude plugin install finance@pace</code>
                </div>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">2</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Authorize your warehouse + Microsoft 365</h5>
                <p>Snowflake / Databricks / BigQuery for the ledger pull; Microsoft 365 for Excel writeback. Custom URL prompts on first run.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">3</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Create the monthly routine</h5>
                <p>In Cowork, open <strong>Routines</strong>, preset schedules don't include "last business day of the month." Create the routine with the closest preset, then run <code>/schedule update</code> in the CLI to set a cron expression like <code>0 8 28-31 * 1-5</code> (8am, last few weekdays of the month).</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">4</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Paste this as the routine prompt</h5>
                <PromptBlock prompt={`Run the month-end close in order:

  1. close-management to orchestrate the checklist.
  2. reconciliation against the warehouse ledger
     (call out any unreconciled balance).
  3. variance-analysis vs plan + prior month.
  4. journal-entry-prep for any accruals or
     reclasses the variance analysis surfaces.

Use plan mode for the journal entries : do NOT post
anything to the GL automatically. The controller will
review and approve each entry. Post a close-progress
summary to #finance-close.`} />
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">5</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Manually run for this month's close to verify</h5>
                <p>Click <strong>Run now</strong> at the end of this month. Walk through the journal entries in plan mode; approve, edit, or reject each. Once you trust the output, the routine fires on the last business day automatically.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="usecase-card">
        <h3>Variance you'll have to explain, surfaced before the CFO asks</h3>
        <dl class="usecase-meta">
          <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Routine, schedule, daily 06:00 after nightly close</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>variance-analysis</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Routines (cloud schedule), warehouse connector, threshold alerting, Slack DM to the CFO's prep channel</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p>Every nightly close, the variance skill compares actuals vs plan, flags anything > 5% deviation, drafts the why, and DMs the CFO's prep channel by 7am. The morning standup starts with answers, not surprises.</p>
              <div class="usecase-setup">

                <h4 class="usecase-setup-title">How to set it up</h4>

                <ol class="usecase-steps">

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">1</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Create the scheduled routine in Cowork</h5>

                      <p>In Cowork, open <strong>Routines</strong> &rarr; <strong>New routine</strong> &rarr; <strong>Schedule</strong>. Match the cadence described in the trigger above.</p>

                    </div>

                  </li>

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">2</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Paste this as the routine prompt</h5>

                      <PromptBlock prompt={`Every weekday at 6am after the nightly close, pull yesterday's actuals from the warehouse and compare against plan. Flag any P&L line item more than 5% off plan.

For each flagged variance, draft the explanation: the underlying driver (what category of activity changed), supporting data (which slice moved), and one sentence the CFO can repeat in the morning meeting.

DM the digest to the CFO's prep channel by 7am.`} label="Variance prep prompt" />

                    </div>

                  </li>

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">3</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Click <strong>Run now</strong> to verify</h5>

                      <p>Eyeball the first run for accuracy. Once it looks right, the routine fires on its trigger from then on. Assumes the plugin from the marquee above is already installed and connectors authorized.</p>

                    </div>

                  </li>

                </ol>

              </div>
      </article>

      <article class="usecase-card">
        <h3>Vendor contract triage with your playbook in the loop</h3>
        <dl class="usecase-meta">
          <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Routine, API trigger fired by Box / Egnyte webhook on new-file</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>review-contract</code>, <code>vendor-check</code>, <code>vendor-review</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Routines (API trigger), Box/Egnyte connector, in-house playbook context, plan mode</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p>Any new vendor contract dropped in the legal folder triggers a playbook-aware review: <code>review-contract</code> walks payment terms, auto-renewal language, liability caps, and data clauses; <code>vendor-check</code> and <code>vendor-review</code> add the procurement-side perspective. Findings post as a checklist. Legal + Finance both see what to fight for before the call.</p>
              <div class="usecase-setup">

                <h4 class="usecase-setup-title">How to set it up</h4>

                <ol class="usecase-steps">

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">1</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Create the API-triggered routine</h5>

                      <p>In Cowork, open <strong>Routines</strong> &rarr; <strong>New routine</strong> &rarr; <strong>API</strong>. Save and copy the routine URL + bearer token; point the upstream webhook at it (e.g. calendar provider, Intercom webhook, PagerDuty webhook, depending on the trigger).</p>

                    </div>

                  </li>

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">2</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Paste this as the routine prompt</h5>

                      <PromptBlock prompt={`When a vendor MSA hits the procurement intake, run contract-review against our playbook (standard payment terms, liability caps, IP assignment, termination, MFN, data processing addendum if PII is involved). Produce a redlined version with explanations next to each change.

Park the redline in plan mode for legal sign-off. Once approved, post a one-paragraph summary to #procurement for the requesting team.`} label="Vendor MSA review prompt" />

                    </div>

                  </li>

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">3</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Click <strong>Run now</strong> to verify</h5>

                      <p>Eyeball the first run for accuracy. Once it looks right, the routine fires on its trigger from then on. Assumes the plugin from the marquee above is already installed and connectors authorized.</p>

                    </div>

                  </li>

                </ol>

              </div>
      </article>

      <article class="usecase-card">
        <h3>AP batch processor: invoices into journal entries, on a Friday cadence</h3>
        <p>Friday afternoon, the routine pulls the week's accounts-payable batch from your accounting system, generates the journal entries with the right GL coding, flags anything unusual (new vendor, unusual amount, missing PO), and stages everything for controller approval. Monday morning, the controller approves the batch in 15 minutes instead of an hour.</p>
        <dl class="usecase-meta">
          <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Routine, schedule, weekly Friday 17:00</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>journal-entry-prep</code>, <code>variance-analysis</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Routines (cloud schedule), QuickBooks connector, plan mode for controller approval</dd></div>
        </dl>
              <div class="usecase-setup">

                <h4 class="usecase-setup-title">How to set it up</h4>

                <ol class="usecase-steps">

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">1</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Create the scheduled routine in Cowork</h5>

                      <p>In Cowork, open <strong>Routines</strong> &rarr; <strong>New routine</strong> &rarr; <strong>Schedule</strong>. Match the cadence described in the trigger above.</p>

                    </div>

                  </li>

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">2</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Paste this as the routine prompt</h5>

                      <PromptBlock prompt={`Every Friday at 5pm, pull this week's accounts-payable batch from QuickBooks. Generate journal entries with the right GL coding. Flag anything unusual: new vendor (no prior payments), amount more than 2x the trailing-3-month average for that vendor, missing PO reference.

Stage everything in plan mode for the controller to approve Monday morning. Post a one-line summary to #finance-close.`} label="AP batch journal-entry prompt" />

                    </div>

                  </li>

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">3</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Click <strong>Run now</strong> to verify</h5>

                      <p>Eyeball the first run for accuracy. Once it looks right, the routine fires on its trigger from then on. Assumes the plugin from the marquee above is already installed and connectors authorized.</p>

                    </div>

                  </li>

                </ol>

              </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <footer class="usecases-footer">
      <p>
        Have a finance workflow that should live here? <a href="https://github.com/GoldenBerry-SO/Pace/issues/new">Open an issue</a> with the trigger, skills, and Claude features it uses; we'll fold it into the cookbook.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .usecases-page {
    max-width: var(--width-content);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--spacing-xl) var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-3xl);
  }
  .usecases-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecases-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .usecases-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-3xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .usecases-lede {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .usecases-lede strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  /* Engineering callout above the TOC */
  .usecases-eng-callout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
    align-items: center;
    background: var(--color-forest);
    color: var(--color-paper);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-paper);
    opacity: 0.78;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-eyebrow::before {
    content: "";
    display: inline-block;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: currentColor;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-text h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.4vw, 1.7rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--color-paper);
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-text p {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-paper);
    opacity: 0.85;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 56ch;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 12px 20px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-radius: 2px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform var(--duration-base) var(--ease-out-quart);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-cta:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .usecases-eng-callout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      padding: var(--spacing-md);
    }
  }

  /* TOC grid */
  .usecases-toc {
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
  }
  .usecases-toc-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-ash);
    display: block;
    margin: 0 6px var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .usecases-toc-grid {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .usecases-toc-grid a {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    transition: border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart),
                background var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart),
                transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .usecases-toc-grid a:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-forest);
    background: var(--color-forest-dim);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  .usecases-toc-name {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-toc-count {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--color-ash);
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .usecases-toc-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  .usecases-team {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
    scroll-margin-top: 96px;
  }
  .usecases-team-head {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecases-team-head h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }
  .usecases-team-tagline {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .usecase-card {
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .usecase-card-marquee {
    border-color: var(--color-forest);
    background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--color-paper-elev) 92%, var(--color-forest-dim));
  }
  .usecase-card-badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 4px 8px;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .usecase-card-badge::before {
    content: "";
    display: inline-block;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: currentColor;
  }
  .usecase-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.022em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .usecase-card > p {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md);
  }
  /* Meta: small chip row at the bottom (was a big dl block at top) */
  .usecase-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px 8px;
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0 0;
    padding-top: var(--spacing-md);
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecase-meta > div {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 4px 10px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }
  .usecase-meta dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-ash);
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .usecase-meta dt::after {
    content: ":";
    margin-left: 1px;
    color: var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecase-meta dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    font-size: 11px;
  }
  .usecase-meta dd code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    background: transparent;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
  }
  .usecase-card p {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .usecase-card p code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-code-border);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-footer {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-2xl);
    padding-top: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .usecases-footer a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch p {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch a,
  .usecases-impeccable-when a,
  .usecases-team-tagline a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch code,
  .usecases-impeccable-when code,
  .usecases-team-tagline code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-code-border);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-cta {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--spacing-sm);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-cta .cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 10px 18px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: background var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart), color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .cta-primary {
    background: var(--color-forest);
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }
  .cta-primary:hover {
    background: var(--color-forest-hover);
  }
  .cta-secondary {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .cta-secondary:hover {
    background: var(--color-forest-dim);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when {
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when summary {
